.TH "ROARK\-AGENT\-PROMPT\-UPDATE" "1" "" "roark-agent-prompt-update" "Roark Analytics API Manual"
.SH "NAME"
roark\-agent\-prompt\-update \- Set an agent's prompt
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark agent prompt update
\fIagent\-id\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Sets the agent's API\-managed prompt. This is its own version history (`source: API_MANAGED`), separate from prompts observed on calls, edited in the app, or managed by config\-as\-code. Setting the same content twice is a no\-op (no new version). Roark does not run your agent and no metric reads this prompt: it is stored and versioned for your reference.
.SH "API"
PUT /v1/agent/{agentId}/prompts
.SH "ARGUMENTS"
.TP
\fIagent\-id\fR
The agent\-id.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-prompt\fR \fI<value>\fR
The prompt content to set. Required.
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-data\fR \fI<json>\fR
Request body as JSON, or @file to read one (@\- for stdin).
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-input\fR
Never prompt; fail instead.
.TP
\fB\-\-base\-url\fR \fI<url>\fR
API base URL.
.TP
\fB\-\-token\fR \fI<token>\fR
Bearer token. Prefer ROARK_API_BEARER_TOKEN or the stored credential.
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<ms>\fR
Request timeout in milliseconds.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-retries\fR \fI<count>\fR
Retries for retryable failures.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<format>\fR
Output format: auto, json, jsonl, plain.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Shorthand for \-\-format json.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable colour.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress non\-essential output.
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-project\-base\-url\fR
Send the stored credential to a base URL set by a project .roark.json. Refused by default.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
roark agent prompt update <agent\-id> \-\-prompt <value>
.fi
.RE
